    fix(harness): the adapter verdict counts WARN rows — an UNVERIFIED adapter no longer prints PASS. Addresses CF-141.
    
    Measured at d4f2600: every shipped adapter ended with
      [ "$FAILED" -eq 0 ] && { say "X: PASS"; exit 0; } || { say "X: FAIL ($FAILED)"; exit 1; }
    and lib.sh's warn() counted nothing, so an adapter whose own banner says `UNVERIFIED adapter`
    printed `OPENCODE: PASS` and exited 0 beside two WARN rows (user_space_binary, non_interactive).
    That contradicts specs/HARNESS.md ("an unverified installer must say so out loud") and made the
    PRD's CF-106 cell ungradeable.
    
    Scripts
    - scripts/lib.sh: warn() increments a WARNED counter (signature and row format unchanged, so the
      ~40 other callers keep working); new verdict() prints ONE line from the row counts and returns
      the status the caller exits with — `FAIL (n)` / 1, `UNVERIFIED` / 3, `PASS` / 0. One
      implementation, so six adapters cannot drift.
    - All six adapters (opencode, hermes, claude-code, codex, pi-agent, deepseek) end at verdict(),
      and every early death reaches it: install-hermes.sh refusing an out-of-range interpreter now
      prints `FAIL python — …` AND `HERMES: FAIL (1)` instead of exiting 1 with no verdict, so a
      caller can tell a verdict from a crash.
    - The certification rule is the --check rule. The modes that ACT (--apply, --turn, --app-server)
      pass `action`: there a WARN is advice about a run that already happened (a $HOME/.local/bin PATH
      hint, an [experimental] app-server) and does not unmake a measured install, so only FAIL rows
      decide. Without that split install-codex.sh --apply — a measured ladder — would report
      UNVERIFIED for a successful install.
    
    Tests (AGENTS.md rule 2 — every check must be able to fail)
    - tests/selftest.sh §59 (new, one numbered section): ONE stub-adapter fixture, three arms that
      differ only in the rows it prints — WARN -> `STUB: UNVERIFIED` exit 3 and never PASS, FAIL ->
      `STUB: FAIL (1)` exit 1, all PASS -> `STUB: PASS` exit 0 — plus the row's own probe against the
      real install-opencode.sh --check (`OPENCODE: UNVERIFIED`, exit 3), the PRE-FIX adapter at
      d4f2600 on the same stub printing `OPENCODE: PASS` exit 0 as the red control (so §59's green
      depends on this change), a verdict-versus-row-count check over all six adapters, and the
      hermes interpreter refusal.
    - Proofs that asserted the superseded contract now assert the row-count one, same fixtures:
      tests/harness/opencode-install-test.sh (C1/D1/E1/F1 exit 3 + UNVERIFIED; H1 pins the all-PASS
      case), tests/harness/codex-install-test.sh B5, tests/harness/claude-code-install-test.sh (post
      --apply --check), tests/harness-node-e2e.sh arm 1 (a verdict line consistent with the rows, so
      an adapter that prints rows and dies has no verdict and fails), tests/harness-conformance.sh
      (an exit-3 leg names its WARN rows instead of "no FAIL row printed").
    
    Docs
    - specs/HARNESS.md: new "The verdict line" — the vocabulary, the row-count rule, UNVERIFIED = exit
      3 (same status verify-node.sh uses for an unverified manifest), the action-mode split, and the
      two lines that are deliberately not verdicts (usage refusals exit 2 with a named reason;
      claude-code --turn without a credential exits 3 as SKIP).
    - docs/PRD-code-factory.md CF-106 now CITES the §59 arms instead of describing the legs; the row
      set half stays open and is named as open.
    - docs/handbook/chapters/M5-harness.md §6 gains M5-C3 (the adapter -> caller verdict contract, with
      its producer/consumer and state) and §7 gains the two §59 arms. The RED field count line is
      untouched: this change removes no red.
    - docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md: the §59 mapping row, and the plan's own section census — it claimed 57
      numbered sections / 61 arms while the tree carried 58/61, and was already drifting on the
      §57->§58 landing; corrected to 59/62 with the tree (cf198: RESULT: OK, arms_plan=62 arms_tree=62;
      cf099 --sections-only: plan_sections=59 selftest_sections=59).
    
    Evidence
    - bash -n clean on every changed script.
    - The row's probe: `OPENCODE: UNVERIFIED`, rc=3, two WARN rows (was `OPENCODE: PASS`, rc=0).
    - bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS, exit 0, 59 numbered sections, §59's seven PASS rows.
    - bash scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK (7 warning(s), all pre-existing).
    - tests/harness/{opencode,codex,claude-code}-install-test.sh and tests/harness-node-e2e.sh -> PASS.
    - bash docs/audits/cf198-section-mapping.sh -> RESULT: OK; handbook_spine.py -> findings=0.
    
